    "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nPrefix-cache aware routing needs the full KV cache spec for each group. `get_kv_cache_group_metadata()` only gives kind, block size and sliding window, so this PR fills in the rest.\r\n\r\n- Each group now includes layer names/count, heads, head size, dtype, page size and the MLA, sink and mamba fields\r\n- `UniformTypeKVCacheSpecs` groups list their per-layer specs under `layer_specs` so no detail gets lost\r\n- Added `get_kv_cache_group_metadata_async` on the core client and wired it through `EngineClient`/`AsyncLLM`. The result is cached after the first call\r\n\r\nThis builds on #56925 which brought the method back after #53941 removed it and fixed block sizes under DCP. Block sizes still come from the scheduler's manager, so DCP groups keep reporting the effective size. \r\n\r\nRef: \"Required core change\" in RFC ##38147 description.\r\n\r\nPartial #38147\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n`pytest -s -v tests/v1/engine/test_kv_cache_group_metadata.py`\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\nAll tests pass.\r\n",
