    {
      "body": "@njhill @pavanimajety FYI, this builds on #56925.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-05T10:51:09Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/48121#issuecomment-5992978565",
      "id": 5992978565,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-05T10:51:09Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "hickeyma"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "> Personally, I feel that the canonical KV cache group metadata is too low-level to expose outside the vLLM system; we'll probably be tweaking it quite often.\r\n\r\n@noooop sorry for the slow reply. You're right and the spec has changed a lot since I opened this\r\n\r\nI'll cut the PR down as follows:\r\n\r\n- drop the layout fields (heads, head size, dtype, page size, mamba shapes, layer names, per-layer specs)\r\n- keep the existing `kind` / `block_size` / `sliding_window` per group which is what Dynamo already gets\r\n- keep the `EngineClient` / `AsyncLLM` wiring so the frontend can reach it\r\n\r\nFor capacity the plugin can read `kv_cache_size_tokens`, `kv_cache_max_concurrency` and `effective_attention_block_size` from `CacheConfig`, so nothing new is needed there. That covers what llm-d reads today from `vllm:cache_config_info`.\r\n\r\nSo the PR ends up as plumbing only with no new fields exposed. Does that work for you?\r\n\r\n@njhill would you be ok with that scope? I'll rebase and push the trimmed version.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-13T11:33:33Z",
